From 037f191c82b5e7b40c83d04eb0d93e313ec85466 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 10:39:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05778/11362] [outer-loop] add
 live_llm_inference_local_gguf_sota substrate; fix uppercase MODEL_SPECS
 recognition

User asked to dig into two DURATION_TOO_SHORT flags from .481: exp5262
(solver-grounded constraint extraction, 56.3s) and exp5263 (neuron/
attention-energy hallucination probe, 23.7s). Both are honest,
non-fabricated negative results -- exp5262 found constraint_validity_rate
0.25 vs a 0.5 baseline (no useful oracle-distinct signal), exp5263 found
a null logit-energy signal_delta=0.0048 -- but both got flagged because
no substrate category recognized "a handful of short local-SOTA-GGUF
generation calls, or logit/logprob forward passes over a bounded fixture
set, not full multi-hundred-token generation."

This is the fifth time this exact bug class has appeared this week: a
genuinely new, legitimate substrate shape with no existing category.
Added live_llm_inference_local_gguf_sota as a recognized substrate
(10.0s floor -- comfortably below both real observations of 23.7s/56.3s,
well above what a genuine local-GGUF model load could plausibly complete
in), wired ahead of the generic live_llm_inference check in
duration_floor_for_artifact(). Unlike prior no-LLM substrate additions,
this one is genuinely LLM inference, so model_specs/target_model stays
required (not exempted) in check_methodology_present.

While investigating, also found and fixed a second, separate issue: both
artifacts declare their model info under an uppercase MODEL_SPECS key
(a Python-constant-style name) rather than lowercase model_specs -- and
check_methodology_present only recognized the lowercase form. Checked
corpus-wide: 24 artifacts use the uppercase variant, not just these two.
Fixed to recognize either casing.

10 new tests (tests/python/test_adversarial_verify_local_sota_gguf_small_n_
substrate.py): recognition-function coverage, floor-priority, exact
exp5262/exp5263 reproductions now clean, a fabricated-near-instant-claim
regression guard, a full-generation-still-needs-60s-floor regression
guard, a model-specs-still-required regression guard (this substrate is
genuinely LLM inference, unlike the no-LLM substrates), and an
uppercase-MODEL_SPECS-recognized regression guard. Full suite (277
tests) green. Corpus-wide dry-run sanity check unchanged (5 previously-
known qualifying artifacts, no new flood).

Un-quarantined both artifacts: 0 CRITICAL flags each (was 1 each). Each
has one remaining WARN (missing random_seed) -- genuinely absent from
these conductor-authored artifacts, left as an honest, non-blocking gap
rather than backfilled by the outer-loop. Both artifacts' own test
suites (14 tests) still pass after patching, confirming no checksum
invalidation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
